pth\"] = max(stats[\"max_wave_depth\"], sim[\"wave_depth\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/24/code.py:423:    - Then repeatedly activate any 4-neighbor-adjacent wall-colored seeds. Each activated seed disappears from its original cell, slides by the same center-seeking rule, turns yellow, and may trigger another wave.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/24/code.py:451:        \"max_wave_depth\": int(combo_stats[\"max_wave_depth\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/24/code.py:865:                \"wave_depth\": best_sim[\"wave_depth\"],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/3/code.py:23:#    simultaneous first wave, because that shot already existed. Using the continued 10-step landing is the minimal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/3/code.py:29:#    - Output is no longer determined only by first-wave 5-step landings; continuation shots may add both sprite hits and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/3/code.py:31:#    - Generator samples that merely contain first-wave hits would silently regress to the original task, so the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/3/code.py:50:#    appear beyond the first-wave 5-step targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/3/code.py:280:    - The first-wave geometry is unchanged, but the visible output is not a one-pass lookup anymore. You must recover each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/13/code.py:3:# Name: 交叉标记+链式反应\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:36:#    wave sources while still showing the three essential changes together:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:63:#    few square wavefronts, so there is no dense overpainting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:134:    Repaint each wall-bounded region as sparse square waves that spread out from the markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/co